ask greet(name)
What's your name?
Nice to meet you, Ada

TRUE:
  name = "Ada"

  Because greet("Ada") is satisfied by:
    greet(name) if print("What's your name?") AND read(name) AND concat("Nice to meet you, ", name, message) AND print(message)

  Variable bindings:
    name = "Ada"
    message = "Nice to meet you, Ada"

  Proof:
    print("What's your name?") is true (built-in).
    read("Ada") is true (built-in).
    concat("Nice to meet you, ", "Ada", "Nice to meet you, Ada") is true (built-in).
    print("Nice to meet you, Ada") is true (built-in).

ask tip(bill, amount)
How much was the bill?
A 15% tip is 6.375

TRUE:
  bill = 42.5
  amount = 6.375

  Because tip(42.5, 6.375) is satisfied by:
    tip(bill, amount) if print("How much was the bill?") AND read_number(bill) AND amount = bill * 0.15 AND print("A 15% tip is", amount)

  Variable bindings:
    bill = 42.5
    amount = 6.375

  Proof:
    print("How much was the bill?") is true (built-in).
    read_number(42.5) is true (built-in).
    amount = 42.5 * 0.15 = 6.375 (calculated).
    print("A 15% tip is", 6.375) is true (built-in).

